//! Declares the app ACL for the `generate_handler!` commands in `src/lib.rs`.
//!
//! Without an app manifest, Tauri checks no capability before running a
//! command that is not a plugin's, so any window on a local origin could call
//! every command. With one, Tauri refuses an app command unless a capability
//! grants it to the calling window and origin. `tauri-build` writes an
//! `allow-<command>` and a `deny-<command>` permission for each name below
//! into `permissions/autogenerated` (not tracked), and
//! `capabilities/default.json` grants the allow permissions to the `main`
//! window only. The tests in `src/lib.rs` check that this list, the
//! capability and `generate_handler!` name the same commands.

